## Objective
- Passive security assessment of signageOS bug bounty program targeting `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`
- Identify reportable vulnerabilities (real logic flaws with concrete POC) while respecting scope exclusions and passive-only testing constraints

## Important Details
- **Eligible targets (ONLY)**: `box.signageos.io`, `api.signageos.io`
- **Excluded classes**: DoS, descriptive errors/headers, public file disclosure, outdated libs, OPTIONS/TRACE, CSRF on logout/anonymous forms, cookie flags, self-XSS, scanner reports without POC, physical access, social engineering, username enumeration, brute-force/lockout, SSL/TLS, clickjacking w/o exploit, mail config, known-vulnerable lib w/o signageOS-specific exploit, password/account-recovery policies, autocomplete, public login panels, email verification gaps, session control on email/password change
- **Reportable focus**: Real logic flaws (IDOR/authz/business logic/SSRF-type) with concrete POC on eligible hosts
- **Passive-first constraint**: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification
- **Secrets handling**: sha256 only, never raw
- **Auth system**: Auth0 OAuth2 on box; dual-auth on api (JWT Bearer + X-Auth `id:unsafeDecryptedToken` format)
- **API route map**: 40+ v1 paths mapped from bundle.js; all JWT/X-Auth-gated (403)
- **X-Auth error taxonomy**: 403074 (MISSING_ACCOUNT_ID), 403075 (MISSING_ACCOUNT_CLIENT_SECRET), 403076 (WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET), 403105 (WRONG_JWT_TOKEN)
- **Error text serves dual purpose**: Excluded as "descriptive errors" BUT simultaneously provides mechanism evidence for IDOR hypothesis

## Work State
### Completed
- **box.signageos.io/status** (MISCONFIG, conf 96, PASSIVE): POC finalized 30+ cycles — unauthenticated JSON leak of pod hostname (rs `box-54846c877b`), 64-hex process.uid, Node v20.20.2, 9-service topology (amqp0/redis0-3/mongoDB0-3) + cpuUsage/memoryUsage; secgrep=0 (only x-powered-by: Express + CloudFront); evidence archive body sha256 `38737948…`/headers `b11ba5ba…`
- **box.signageos.io / + /login/ CORS+CSP** (MISCONFIG, conf 92, PASSIVE): 17 static ACAO values (incl `http://` plaintext + `https://*.zdusercontent.com` wildcard + `api.signageos.io` sibling + path-bearing recaptcha), 0 access-control-allow-credentials, evil.test NOT reflected (static whitelist); CSP 59+ origins with triplicated Auth0 oauth/token; 6 rotating nonces on SPA routes; entry hardened (secgrep=4) vs /status bare (secgrep=0)
- **api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token** (IDOR, conf 86, AUTH_HELPED): 403074 errorDetail byte-identical across rs rotations; org identity from X-Auth header first-part before `:` while path `{uid}` is client-supplied — cross-tenant IDOR mechanism confirmed; zero auth drift across rs `77955558bc`→`7c5fdc9777`; zero ACAO under evil.test on 403
- **api.signageos.io/status** (MISCONFIG, conf ~85): Hardened with HSTS/xfo/xcto/no-store (secgrep=3), zero ACAO, but still leaks hostname/uid/Node v24.19.0/topology; differential vs box /status persists
- **api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/device-plan-history** (IDOR, conf 50, AUTH_HELPED): Route exists, JWT-gated (403105) pre-auth — mechanism-family (client-supplied {uid}) intact
- **api.signageos.io/v1/company/{uid}/support-access-permission** (IDOR, conf 45, AUTH_HELPED): PUT route exists, JWT-gated (403) pre-auth
- **CONFIRMED DEAD**: videowall-designer leaked clientId/secret (sha256 `564c293b…`) tested as X-Auth on prod → 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET "Account not found"; staging-only fixture, credential reuse disproven
- **REJECTED classes** (never report): descriptive errors, pre-auth IDOR (all 403 JWT-gated), CORS credential-theft (0 creds flag), Auth0 OAuth2 (not passively testable), /ready (trivial), WebSocket (302 redirect), all probe paths (healthz/livez/readyz/live/metrics/env/etc → 302 catch-all), bundle.js v2 (zero API paths)
- Replica sets flipped: box `8676fb5f57` → `54846c877b`; api `77955558bc` → `7c5fdc9777`; zero auth drift across flips

### Active
- Monitoring passive surface for changes across K8s pod rotations and rs flips
- IDOR cross-tenant security-token hypothesis maintained at conf 86 (AUTH_HELPED, blocked on credentials)

### Blocked
- **Cross-tenant IDOR verification** (conf 86): Requires valid account with ≥1 org + second org UID → must run `sos login` (Auth0 device-code flow on box.signageos.io) to acquire JWT + X-Auth pair; cannot progress without human-provided credentials
- All 60+ API routes remain 403 JWT/X-Auth-gated — no pre-auth bypass surface found across 30+ cycles

## Next Move
1. **HUMAN**: Run `sos login` (Auth0 device-code flow on box.signageos.io) to obtain valid account owning ≥1 org → acquire JWT + X-Auth `<orgA-id>:<secret>` pair → then test: `curl -s -H "X-Auth: <orgA-id>:<secret>" https://api.signageos.io/v1/organization/<orgB-uid>/security-token` — this is the only way to progress the high-severity IDOR lead (conf 86)
