## Objective
- Passive bug bounty reconnaissance of signageOS program targeting `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io` to identify reportable logic flaws, misconfigurations, and IDOR vulnerabilities per scope.yml rules.

## Important Details
- **Eligible targets ONLY**: `box.signageos.io`, `api.signageos.io`
- **Passive-first**: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification
- **Scope exclusions**: descriptive errors/headers, outdated libs, CSRF on anonymous forms, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, username enumeration, brute-force/lockout, SSL/TLS, clickjacking w/o exploit, public login panels, email verification gaps, session control on email/password change
- **Secrets handling**: sha256 only, never raw
- **Program focus**: real logic flaws (IDOR/authz/business logic/SSRF-type) with concrete POC
- **Auth mechanism (dual)**: JWT Bearer (main API) + X-Auth `id:unsafeDecryptedToken` format for bulk provisioning; org identity derived from X-Auth header first-part before `:`; path `{uid}` is client-supplied
- **Error taxonomy**: 403074 MISSING_ACCOUNT_ID_TO_AUTHENTICATE, 403075 MISSING_ACCOUNT_CLIENT_SECRET, 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET, 403105 WRONG_JWT_TOKEN, NO_ORGANIZATION_TO_AUTHENTICATE

