## Objective
- Conduct passive security reconnaissance on signageOS bug bounty program (targets: `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`) to identify reportable vulnerabilities per scope.yml rules.
- Identify and validate real logic flaws with concrete POCs, operating passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps).

## Important Details
- **Eligible targets**: ONLY `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`
- **Exclusions per scope.yml**: descriptive errors/headers, outdated libs, CSRF on anonymous forms, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, username enumeration, brute-force policies, SSL/TLS, clickjacking w/o exploit, public login panels, email verification gaps, session control on password changes, etc.
- **Passive-first rule**: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification
- **Secrets handling**: SHA256 only, never raw
- **GitHub org**: `signageos` (59 public repos) — videowall-designer had hardcoded clientId/secret (SHA256 `564c293b…`) targeting staging `http://api.kiera.office.signageos.io` — **CONFIRMED DEAD** on prod (403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET)
- **Error taxonomy at api.signageos.io**: 403074 (MISSING_ACCOUNT_ID_TO_AUTHENTICATE), 403075 (NO_ORGANIZATION_TO_AUTHENTICATE), 403076 (WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET_OR_ACCOUNT_IDENTIFICATION), 403105 (WRONG_JWT_TOKEN)
- **Dual auth mechanism**: JWT Bearer (main API) + X-Auth `id:unsafeDecryptedToken` (bulk provisioning); security-token endpoint is X-Auth-only (JWT ignored)
- **RS rotation history**: `6cc9959bb4` → `77955558bc` → `7c5fdc9777` (api), `8676fb5f57` → `54846c877b` → `c877d9cc8` (box) — zero auth drift across all rotations

