## Objective
- Passive security assessment of signageOS bug bounty program targeting `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`
- Identify real logic flaws (IDOR, authz, business logic, SSRF) with concrete POCs on eligible hosts

## Important Details
- **Scope**: Only `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io` are eligible targets
- **Exclusions**: DoS, descriptive errors, outdated libs, CSRF on anon forms, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, self-XSS, scanner reports without POC, brute-force policies, SSL/TLS, clickjacking w/o exploit, username enumeration, Auth0 OAuth2 redirect_uri/state (not testable passively), CSRF on logout
- **Rules**: Passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps), no account creation, no data modification, sha256 only for secrets
- **Mode**: `{"phase": "POC", "target": "box"}`
- **GitHub org**: `signageos` (59 public repos) — videowall-designer leaked clientId/secret CONFIRMED DEAD (staging-only fixture, 403076 on prod)
- **API dual-auth mechanism**: X-Auth `id:unsafeDecryptedToken` format + JWT Bearer (main API); org identity derived from X-Auth header first-part before `:`, path `{uid}` is client-supplied
- **CloudFront**: Both box and api fronted by CloudFront since ~2026-08-10
- **Replica set rotations tracked**: box went through `7c8c876945→8676fb5f57→54846c877b→c877d9cc8`; api went through `6f69db97d5→6d67cd6668→77955558bc→7c5fdc9777`

## Work State
### Completed
- **box.signageos.io/status** (CONF 97, PASSIVE): Unauthenticated GET returns JSON leaking K8s pod hostname, 64-hex process.uid, Node v20.20.2, 9-service topology (amqp0/redis0-3/mongoDB0-3), cpuUsage/memoryUsage, per-service responseTime. Headers: ONLY `x-powered-by: Express` + CloudFront (secgrep=0). POC finalized 60+ cycles, evidence archived at `artifacts/box-status/` (body sha256, headers sha256). Hardening differential vs `/`+`/login/` (secgrep=4) and api `/status` (secgrep=3) confirmed.
- **box.signageos.io/ + /login/ CORS+CSP** (CONF 92, PASSIVE): 17 static ACAO incl `http://` plaintext + `https://*.zdusercontent.com` wildcard + `api.signageos.io` sibling + path-bearing recaptcha. 0 `access-control-allow-credentials`. evil.test NOT reflected (static whitelist). CSP 59+ origins with triplicated Auth0 oauth/token. 6 rotating x-*-nonce-hash headers. MISCONFIG-only (no credential-theft path).
- **api.signageos.io/status** (CONF ~80, PASSIVE): Hardened (HSTS/xfo/xcto/no-store, secgrep=3), zero ACAO under any Origin. Still leaks hostname/uid/Node v24.19.0/8-svc topology (mongoDB3 absent). Differential vs box /status persists.
- **api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token** (CONF 86, AUTH_HELPED): 403074 errorDetail byte-identical across 7+ rs rotations confirms org identity from X-Auth header first-part, path `{uid}` client-supplied → cross-tenant IDOR mechanism CONFIRMED. JWT Bearer ignored (returns same 403074 as no-header). Zero auth drift.
- **videowall-designer leaked clientId/secret**: CONFIRMED DEAD — staging-only fixture, X-Auth on prod → 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET "Account not found"
- **All other probes fully enumerated and rejected**: box `/ready` (200 "OK"), box WebSocket (302), box `/healthz`/`/livez`/`/readyz`/`/live` (302), api CORS (zero ACAO), api v1/*+v2/* pre-auth IDOR (all 403 JWT/X-Auth-gated), api descriptive errors (excluded per scope), box Auth0 OAuth2 (not testable passively)

### Active
- Monitoring box.signageos.io/status for any hardening changes (60+ cycles stable, zero hardening added)
- Monitoring api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token mechanism across rs rotations (7+ rotations, zero drift)
- Evidence archive at `artifacts/box-status/` maintained across workspace resets

### Blocked
- **IDOR cross-tenant verification** (conf 86, AUTH_HELPED): Requires valid credentials — `sos login` (Auth0 device-code flow on box.signageos.io) → obtain account JWT + X-Auth pair from two different orgs → test `curl -s -H "X-Auth: <orgA-id>:<secret>" https://api.signageos.io/v1/organization/<orgB-uid>/security-token`
- No passive bypass possible for api.signageos.io v1/*+v2/* endpoints (all 60+ routes 403 JWT/X-Auth-gated)
- No new unauthenticated surface discovered on box beyond /status + CORS/CSP (all other paths → 302 login catch-all)

## Next Move
1. **HUMAN action needed**: Run `sos login` (Auth0 device-code flow) on box.signageos.io to obtain valid account with ≥1 organization → capture JWT + X-Auth pair → test cross-tenant security-token access with two different org credentials
2. Continue monitoring box.signageos.io/status for any hardening additions or field changes (prior version/cpuUsage/memoryUsage fields were temporarily absent ~2026-08-18)

