## Objective
- Perform passive-only security assessment of signageOS bug bounty program on two eligible hosts (`box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`), identifying real logic flaws with concrete POCs for submission.

## Important Details
- **Eligible targets ONLY**: `box.signageos.io`, `api.signageos.io`
- **Phase**: POC phase, targeting `box` host
- **Passive-first**: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification
- **Scope exclusions**: DoS, descriptive errors/headers, public file/dir disclosure, outdated libs, OPTIONS/TRACE, CSRF on logout/anonymous forms, cookie flags non-sensitive, self-XSS, scanner reports without POC, physical access, social engineering, username enumeration, brute-force/lockout policies, SSL/TLS best practices + attacks, clickjacking w/o exploit, mail config, known-vulnerable lib w/o signageOS exploit, password/account-recovery policies, autocomplete, public login panels, email verification gaps, session control on email/password changes
- **Secrets in commits**: SHA256 only, never raw
- **Latest box replica set**: `box-59b5ffd68b` (rotated from `box-c877d9cc8`)
- **Latest api replica set**: `api-7c5fdc9777`
- **GitHub org**: `signageos` (59 public repos)
- **Both hosts behind CloudFront** (confirmed since ~2026-08-10)

## Work State
### Completed
- **box.signageos.io/status INFO LEAK (CONF 97)**: Unauthenticated GET returns JSON leaking K8s pod hostname, 64-hex process.uid, Node v20.20.2, 9-service topology (amqp0/redis0-3/mongoDB0-3), cpuUsage/memoryUsage, per-service responseTime. Headers: ONLY `x-powered-by: Express` (secgrep=0). Zero hardening headers across 60+ cycles and 7+ rs rotations. Evidence archived at `artifacts/box-status/` (body sha256 `38737948…`/headers `b11ba5ba…`).
- **box.signageos.io/ + /login/ CORS+CSP (CONF 92)**: 17 static ACAO values including `http://box.signageos.io` plaintext variant, `https://*.zdusercontent.com` wildcard, `api.signageos.io` sibling, path-bearing recaptcha. `evil.test` NOT reflected (static whitelist). 0 `access-control-allow-credentials` → no credential-theft path, MISCONFIG-only. CSP 59+ origins with triplicated Auth0 oauth/token. Entry points hardened (secgrep=4: HSTS/xfo/xcto/CSP/nonces) vs `/status` (secgrep=0).
- **api.signageos.io/status**: Hardened with HSTS/xfo/xcto/no-store (secgrep=3) but still leaks hostname/uid/Node v24.19.0/8-svc topology. Differential vs box /status persists.
- **api.signageos.io CORS**: Zero ACAO on any path under any Origin — not CORS-exploitable.
- **api.signageos.io/v1/*+v2/* pre-auth IDOR**: All 60+ routes 403 JWT/X-Auth-gated, zero ACAO under any Origin — no passive bypass across 60+ cycles.
- **api.signageos.io/v1/* descriptive errors**: 403074/403075/403076/403105 bodies leak account/error detail — excluded per scope.yml; errorDetail retained only as mechanism evidence.
- **api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token IDOR mechanism (CONF 86, AUTH_HELPED)**: 403074 errorDetail byte-identical across 7+ rs rotations confirms org identity derived from X-Auth header first-part before `:` while path `{uid}` is client-supplied. JWT Bearer ignored (returns same 403074 as no-header). Zero auth drift. Requires valid credentials to exploit.
- **videowall-designer leaked clientId/secret**: CONFIRMED DEAD — staging-only fixture (sha256 `564c293b…`), X-Auth on prod → 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET "Account not found"; credential reuse disproven (60+ cycles).
- **box.signageos.io/ready**: 200 "OK" (2 bytes) — trivial health check, not reportable.
- **box.signageos.io probe set** (/healthz /livez /readyz /live /metrics /env /config.json /csp-report /websocket /graphql): all → 302 login catch-all — no unauthenticated surface beyond /status.
- **box.signageos.io/login Auth0 OAuth2**: redirect_uri/state binding not passively testable without tenant/authenticated session.
- **box.signageos.io/status CORS**: Zero ACAO under spoofed Origin — CORS strictly scoped to SPA entry points only.
- **box.signageos.io WebSocket**: wss:// → 302 login redirect — no unauthenticated surface.

### Active
- Monitoring 3 prioritized findings across probe cycles
- IDOR on `api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token` requires AUTH_HELPED credentials to progress

### Blocked
