## Objective
- Conduct passive security reconnaissance and vulnerability assessment on the signageOS bug bounty program, targeting only `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`
- Identify and document reportable misconfigurations, IDORs, and logic flaws with concrete proof-of-concept evidence

## Important Details
- Eligible targets: **ONLY** `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`
- Scope exclusions: DoS, descriptive errors, outdated libs, SSL/TLS, CSRF on anonymous forms, cookie flags, self-XSS, username enumeration, brute-force, clickjacking w/o exploit, public login panels, email verification gaps, etc.
- Reportable focus: real logic flaws (IDOR/authz/business logic/SSRF-type) with concrete POC on eligible hosts
- Passive-first: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification
- Secrets in commits: sha256 only, never raw
- Auth0 OAuth2 login flow; JWT Bearer + X-Auth `id:unsafeDecryptedToken` dual-auth on API
- Both hosts fronted by CloudFront since 2026-08-10

## Work State
### Completed
- **box.signageos.io/status (POC FINALIZED, 60+ cycles)**: Unauthenticated HTTP 200 JSON leaks K8s pod hostname (rotating through rs: box-8676fb5f57 → box-54846c877b → box-c877d9cc8 → box-59b5ffd68b → box-8b6c78cc8), 64-hex process.uid, Node v20.20.2, 9-service topology (amqp0/redis0-3/mongoDB0-3 including mongoDB3), cpuUsage/memoryUsage/responseTime. Headers: ONLY `x-powered-by: Express` + CloudFront (secgrep=0). Differential vs `/`+`/login/` (secgrep=4) and api `/status` (secgrep=3) confirmed. Evidence archived at `artifacts/box-status/`
- **box.signageos.io CORS+CSP (MISCONFIG, conf 92)**: 17 static ACAO values on `/` and `/login/` including `http://box.signageos.io` plaintext variant + `https://*.zdusercontent.com` wildcard + `api.signageos.io` sibling + path-bearing recaptcha value. Zero `access-control-allow-credentials`. `evil.test` NOT reflected (static whitelist). CSP ~59+ distinct connect-src/frame-src origins with triplicated Auth0 oauth/token. No credential-theft path (MISCONFIG-only)
- **api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token (IDOR, conf 86, AUTH_HELPED)**: 403074 errorDetail byte-identical confirms org identity derived from X-Auth header first-part (before `:`) while path `{uid}` is client-supplied. JWT Bearer token confirmed IGNORED (returns same 403074 as no-header). X-Auth/x-oauth-client_id exclusive gating. Zero auth drift across 8+ rs rotations. Needs valid credentials from two orgs to demonstrate cross-tenant access
- **api.signageos.io/status (hardened)**: secgrep=3 (HSTS/xfo/xcto/no-store), zero ACAO, still leaks hostname/uid/Node v24.19.0/8-svc topology. Differential vs box /status persists
- **videowall-designer leaked clientId/secret (CONFIRMED DEAD)**: `fcbbd714b3f794987b1f1a730d52fa31ddbcb51a087919ea47` (sha256 `564c293ba2a1d60dd6e8f508a7ef65400424ae42b80be0ae04498d528a8a774e`) tested as X-Auth on prod → 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET "Account not found"; staging-only fixture targeting `http://api.kiera.office.signageos.io`
- **api.signageos.io auth error taxonomy confirmed**: 403074 (no auth headers), 403075 (x-oauth-client_id only), 403076 (bad pair), 403105 (JWT-only), NO_ORGANIZATION_TO_AUTHENTICATE (X-Auth org-scoped)
- **api.signageos.io route map fully enumerated**: 60+ routes mapped from bundle.js; org-scoped routes (v1/organization, v1/device, v1/applet, v1/account, v1/timing) return NO_ORGANIZATION_TO_AUTHENTICATE; all others 404
- All prior rejections confirmed stable across 60+ cycles (box /ready, probe sets, CORS credential-theft, WebSocket, Auth0 OAuth2, descriptive errors class)

