## Objective
- Conduct passive security reconnaissance and bug bounty testing on signageOS's two eligible targets: `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`, identifying real logic flaws (IDOR, authz, SSRF, business logic) with concrete POCs.

## Important Details
- Program rules (from scope.yml): Only `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io` are eligible
- Passive-first: GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification
- Exclusions: descriptive errors/headers, outdated libs, CSRF on anonymous forms, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, SSL/TLS, clickjacking w/o exploit, username enumeration, brute-force policies, public login panels, email verification gaps, session control on password changes, etc.
- Reportable focus: real logic flaws with concrete POC on the two eligible hosts
- GitHub org `signageos` (59 public repos) — leaked clientId/secret from `videowall-designer` repo confirmed DEAD (staging-only fixture, credential reuse disproven)
- api.signageos.io has dual auth: JWT Bearer (main API) + X-Auth API-key format `id:unsafeDecryptedToken` (bulk provisioning/org-scoped)
- All 60+ api.signageos.io v1/v2 routes return 403 JWT/X-Auth-gated — no pre-auth bypass surface
- Auth0 OAuth2 on box.signageos.io — redirect_uri/state binding not testable passively without tenant access
- Both hosts fronted by CloudFront (confirmed 2026-08-10+)
- Evidence archive at `artifacts/box-status/`

## Work State
### Completed
- **box.signageos.io/status**: POC finalized (60+ cycles) — unauthenticated GET leaks K8s pod hostname, 64-hex process.uid, Node v20.20.2, 9-service topology (amqp0/redis0-3/mongoDB0-3/mongoDB3), cpuUsage/memoryUsage, per-service responseTime; secgrep=0 (only x-powered-by: Express + CloudFront); zero ACAO under spoofed Origin; rs rotation tracked across 7+ replica sets
- **box.signageos.io/ & /login/ CORS+CSP**: 17 static ACAO (incl http://plaintext + *.zdusercontent.com wildcard + api sibling + path-bearing recaptcha), 0 access-control-allow-credentials, evil.test NOT reflected (static whitelist), CSP 59+ origins with triplicated Auth0 oauth/token, hardened entry (secgrep=4) vs /status (secgrep=0) — MISCONFIG-only, no credential-theft path
- **api.signageos.io/status**: Hardened (HSTS/xfo/xcto/no-store, secgrep=3), zero ACAO, still leaks hostname/uid/Node v24.19.0/8-svc topology (mongoDB3 absent) — differential vs box persists
- **api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token IDOR mechanism**: 403074 errorDetail byte-identical confirms org identity derived from X-Auth header first-part before `:` while path `{uid}` is client-supplied; JWT Bearer ignored (returns same 403074); zero auth drift across 7+ rs rotations; AUTH_HELPED conf 86
- **videowall-designer leaked clientId/secret**: CONFIRMED DEAD — staging-only fixture targeting `http://api.kiera.office.signageos.io`, X-Auth on prod → 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET, credential reuse disproven
- **api.signageos.io v1 route map enumerated**: 40+ paths from bundle.js; all 403 JWT/X-Auth-gated; error codes 403074/403075/403076/403105 taxonomy confirmed
- **box.signageos.io /status CORS**: Zero ACAO under spoofed Origin — CORS strictly scoped to SPA entry points only
- All other box paths (/ready, /healthz, /livez, /metrics, /websocket, etc.) confirmed 302 login catch-all or trivial 200 "OK"
- api.signageos.io CORS: zero ACAO on any path — not CORS-exploitable
