## Objective
- Conduct passive security assessment of signageOS bug bounty program (eligible targets: `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io`) to identify reportable logic flaws with concrete POCs, following scope.yml rules and passive-first methodology.

## Important Details
- **Program scope**: Only `box.signageos.io` and `api.signageos.io` are eligible; extensive exclusion list (no DoS, descriptive errors, outdated libs, CSRF on anonymous forms, cookie flags, self-XSS, etc.)
- **Methodology**: Passive-first (GET/HEAD only, ≤1 rps, no account creation, no data modification); secrets only as sha256 hashes
- **Current phase**: `POC` on `box` target (from `{"phase":"POC","target":"box"}`)
- **Key constraint**: All API endpoints are JWT/X-Auth-gated (403); no pre-auth bypass possible passively
- **Box replicas tracked**: `box-8676fb5f57` → `box-54846c877b` → `box-c877d9cc8` → `box-59b5ffd68b` → `box-8b6c78cc8` (current)
- **API replicas tracked**: `6cc9959bb4` → `77955558bc` → `7c5fdc9777` (current)
- Both hosts fronted by CloudFront (x-cache/via/x-amz-cf-pop)
- `api.signageos.io` /status now has hardened headers (HSTS/xfo/xcto/no-store, secgrep=3); `box.signageos.io` /status has zero hardening (secgrep=0) — persistent differential
- CORS on box `/` + `/login/`: 17 static ACAO values (incl `http://` plaintext + `https://*.zdusercontent.com` wildcard + `api.signageos.io`), **0 access-control-allow-credentials** — MISCONFIG-only, not credential-theft exploitable
- CORS on `/status`: zero ACAO under any Origin — strictly scoped to SPA entry points
- videowall-designer leaked clientId/secret tested on prod → CONFIRMED DEAD (staging-only fixture, 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET)

