## Completed Work

### Findings Verified (4 CONFIRMED)

**SEC-1: `box.signageos.io/status` — Information Disclosure** ✅ POC
- Unauthenticated `GET /status` returns JSON: pod hostname (`box-8b6c78cc8-59b5ffd68b-f5rng`), 64-hex `process.uid`, Node v20.20.2, 9-svc topology (amqp0, redis0-3, mongoDB0-3), CPU/mem/responseTime
- secgrep=0 (only `x-powered-by: Express` + CloudFront)
- **60+ reconfirmation cycles** — zero hardening observed
- Evidence archived at `artifacts/box-status/`

**SEC-2: `api.signageos.io/status` — Information Disclosure** ✅ POC
- Leaks hostname/uid/Node v24.19.0/8-svc topology (mongoDB3 absent)
- Hardened: `HSTS/xfo/xcto/no-store` (secgrep=3), 0 ACAO
- Differential vs box confirmed

**SEC-3: `box.signageos.io` CORS+CSP** ✅ POC
- 17 static ACAO on `/` + `/login/` — includes `http://box.signageos.io` (HTTP variant) + `https://*.zdusercontent.com` (wildcard)
- 0 `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials` — blocks cookie theft
- evil.test NOT reflected (static whitelist, not Origin-reflected)
- CSP: 59+ origins; entry hardened (secgrep=4: HSTS/xfo/xcto/CSP/nonces)

**SEC-4: `api.signageos.io/v1/organization/{uid}/security-token` IDOR** ✅ HOLD (needs creds)
- JWT Bearer **IGNORED** (returns same 403074 without)
- X-Auth gating confirmed NOT JWT-based
- Org identity from X-Auth first-part before `:` vs client-supplied path `{uid}`
- **Mechanism intact across 7+ pod rotations** — conf 86

**Videowall-designer clientId/secret** ❌ CONFIRMED DEAD
- Staging-only fixture (sha256 `564c293b…`), X-Auth on prod → 403076 WRONG_ACCOUNT_SECRET

### Infrastructure Mapped
- 60+ endpoints on `api.signageos.io` all return 403 JWT/X-Auth-gated
- Org-scoped routes (`/v1/organization`, `/v1/device`, `/v1/applet`, `/v1/account`, `/v1/timing`) → `NO_ORGANIZATION_TO_AUTHENTICATE`
- WebSocket → 302, `/ready` → 200 "OK", `/healthz`/`/livez`/`/readyz`/`/live`/`/metrics`/`/graphql`/`/openapi.json` → 302

### Passive Surface Exhausted
All 3 hold items (IDOR + authz drift + peer-recovery) require **valid credentials** to verify. Without `sos login` (Auth0 device-code flow), no new passive leads remain.
